\cf0 Script:\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'93 Among all the learner-level sentiment factors, course instructors played an important role in learner\'92s satisfaction for learning in a MOOC environment. The results of the analysis using the gradient boosting tree model and linear models showed high dependence of course instructor with the learner\'92s satisfaction with that course, as predicted by the previous studies. The researchers found that MOOC with instructors who were enthusiastic, had knowledge about the course, had good communication skills and were humorous during discussions were more satisfied by that course and as compared to the professors who merely read from the PowerPoint slides, less engaging, and did not make an appropriate eye contact with the learners in front of camera. Overall, this factor points out that instructors should be engaging and enthusiastic about the course topic to increase learner\'92s satisfaction with that course and hence help institutions provide more courses in other fields based on its performance. \'94\
